  "tagline": "Standards-compliant RDF triplestore with reasoning, connectors and MCP support for GraphRAG.",
  "description": "GraphDB is an RDF database and SPARQL 1.1 engine built on Eclipse RDF4J, descended from Ontotext's OWLIM. It does forward-chaining inference (RDFS, OWL 2 RL/QL and custom rules) at load time, and connectors keep Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, Solr or Lucene indexes in sync for full-text search. Ontotext merged with Semantic Web Company in 2024 to form Graphwise, and GraphDB 11 added GraphQL, an MCP server and LLM integrations aimed at GraphRAG. It is one of the most complete enterprise triplestores, with a free edition for smaller deployments and a commercial cluster for HA.",
