  "strengths": [
    "Mature forward-chaining reasoning over RDFS and OWL 2 profiles with incremental retraction",
    "Connectors keep external full-text indexes synchronized with the graph",
    "Full W3C stack: SPARQL 1.1, SHACL validation, GeoSPARQL, RDF-star",
    "MCP server and LLM integrations make it easy to plug into agent and GraphRAG pipelines"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Cluster replicates data, so dataset size is bounded by a single node",
    "Materialized inference inflates storage and slows bulk loads with complex rulesets",
    "Commercial license required for HA clustering",
    "RDF modeling and SPARQL have a learning curve for property-graph teams"
  ],
